module shell.barkit
# Stable API for subshells and bar styles: the non-singleton shell types an item
# may build on, re-exported from their real locations so an item imports one
# module instead of scraping internal relative paths. Singletons come from
# shell.services (an item must share the shell's live instances, e.g. the one
# notification server). See docs/subshells.md. Each re-exported file resolves its
# own shell.services import, so items share the shell's singletons.
